  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1044 PM CDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nThere is a high chance for the high pressure system to remain the \ndominant weather system across the southern plains for the weekend \nand into early next work week. The center of the high pressure has \nbetter chances than not to shift to the east during this time.\nThis will most likely end the northwest flow across the panhandles \nmaking it less likely for weather system to impact the southern \npanhandles. This would in turn lead to drier weather conditions \nacross the panhandles. The shifting of the high pressure is also to \nmake it more likely for the temperatures to increase for the weekend \nand early next week. \n\nLater mid next week the high pressure system is more likely than not \nto weaken over the souther plains. This opens up the chance for \nmoisture, and thus thunderstorms, to return back to the panhandles. \nThe increase in moisture also brings the potential for cooler \ntemperatures across the panhandles.",
